{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Waiting for .NET Tasks.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Waiting for .NET Tasks.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"waiting for .net tasks waiting for .net tasks","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Waiting for .NET Tasks.md","fileName":"Waiting for .NET Tasks.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Waiting for .NET Tasks","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Waiting for .NET Tasks.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Waiting for .NET Tasks.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"waiting for .net tasks waiting for .net tasks","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Waiting for .NET Tasks.md","fileName":"Waiting for .NET Tasks.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Waiting for .NET Tasks","heading":"Waiting for .NET Tasks","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":".NET can wait for one task, any task in a set, or every task in a set. Synchronous APIs such as `Wait`, `WaitAny`, and `WaitAll` block the calling thread, whereas asynchronous waiting allows the caller to yield until completion.\n\nThe wait shape should match the dependency: continue after the first useful result, after all required results, or after one specific operation. Blocking is especially risky in responsive and server applications because it consumes a thread and may participate in a deadlock.\n\nThe `WhenAny` and `WhenAll` methods return tasks and therefore compose with awaiting, whereas `WaitAny`, `WaitAll`, and `Wait` synchronously occupy the calling thread. The distinction matters even when both variants eventually identify the same completions.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Waiting for .NET Tasks.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Waiting for .NET Tasks.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"waiting for .net tasks waiting for .net tasks","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Waiting for .NET Tasks.md","fileName":"Waiting for .NET Tasks.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Waiting for .NET Tasks","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]\n[[hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}